<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" xmlns:bioc="http://bpmn.io/schema/bpmn/biocolor/1.0" xmlns:color="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/non-normative/color/1.0" id="ao_defs" targetNamespace="https://github.com/shawngggg/ria-custody-platform">
<bpmn:collaboration id="ao_collab">
<bpmn:participant id="ao_main" name="Custody operations platform (synthetic reference implementation)" processRef="ao_process" />
<bpmn:participant id="ao_req" name="RIA advisor (submits client-signed applications and documents)" />
<bpmn:participant id="ao_svc" name="Identity verification, PEP and adverse media services" />
<bpmn:messageFlow id="ao_msg0" name="Application" sourceRef="ao_req" targetRef="ao_s" />
<bpmn:messageFlow id="ao_msg1" name="Returned: not eligible" sourceRef="ao_e0" targetRef="ao_req" />
<bpmn:messageFlow id="ao_msg2" name="Correction request" sourceRef="ao_t3" targetRef="ao_req" />
<bpmn:messageFlow id="ao_msg3" name="Corrections" sourceRef="ao_req" targetRef="ao_ie" />
<bpmn:messageFlow id="ao_msg4" name="Decline notice" sourceRef="ao_ed" targetRef="ao_req" />
<bpmn:messageFlow id="ao_msg5" name="Account details" sourceRef="ao_e" targetRef="ao_req" />
<bpmn:messageFlow id="ao_msg6" name="Identity check" sourceRef="ao_b1" targetRef="ao_svc" />
<bpmn:messageFlow id="ao_msg7" name="Screening request" sourceRef="ao_t5" targetRef="ao_svc" />
<bpmn:textAnnotation id="ao_ann0"><bpmn:text>Path A: a pure RIA account under a reliance-eligible RIA, using only RIA-provided information. Path B: the client&#39;s self-directed account, or any account under an RIA that isn&#39;t reliance-eligible. Reliance doesn&#39;t shift accountability: the custodian stays responsible for its AML program, SARs, and sanctions.</bpmn:text></bpmn:textAnnotation>
<bpmn:textAnnotation id="ao_ann1"><bpmn:text>Entity accounts add formation and registration documents, operating agreement, memorandum and articles of association.</bpmn:text></bpmn:textAnnotation>
<bpmn:textAnnotation id="ao_ann2"><bpmn:text>Identity that can't be verified follows the CIP failure procedure: request more documents, then decline.</bpmn:text></bpmn:textAnnotation>
<bpmn:textAnnotation id="ao_ann5"><bpmn:text>A registered principal on the RIA service team (Series 24 or 9/10) accepts the account, never someone who prepared the case.</bpmn:text></bpmn:textAnnotation>
<bpmn:messageFlow id="ao_msg8" name="Decline notice" sourceRef="ao_ep" targetRef="ao_req" />
<bpmn:textAnnotation id="ao_ann3"><bpmn:text>Regulatory items hold the account: the client&#39;s signature, the LPOA, CIP information, entity documents, and CDD. A missing fee authorization or tax form doesn&#39;t: the account opens restricted (DOCS: no trading or fee deduction) until it arrives.</bpmn:text></bpmn:textAnnotation>
<bpmn:textAnnotation id="ao_ann4"><bpmn:text>Undoing an acceptance: rescission is for a regulatory issue or an acceptance made before the review, and the restriction is immediate. A non-regulatory document found wrong after opening is reopened instead: the account stays open, restricted (DOCS), and an operational risk event is logged.</bpmn:text></bpmn:textAnnotation>
</bpmn:collaboration>
<bpmn:process id="ao_process" name="Client account opening (paths A and B)" isExecutable="false">
<bpmn:laneSet id="ao_laneset">
<bpmn:lane id="ao_lane_ops" name="Custody operations (first line)">
<bpmn:flowNodeRef>ao_s</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
<bpmn:flowNodeRef>ao_e0</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
<bpmn:flowNodeRef>ao_t3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
<bpmn:flowNodeRef>ao_ie</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
<bpmn:flowNodeRef>ao_ca1</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
<bpmn:flowNodeRef>ao_g3b</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
<bpmn:flowNodeRef>ao_es</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
</bpmn:lane>
